.TH CHPC-ANSIBLE-HELPER 1 "2026-09-29" "CHPC_ansible_helper 0.1.0" "Coastal HPC"
.SH NAME
chpc-ansible-helper \- build Ansible playbooks for airgapped RHEL/Rocky/Debian systems from a vetted template library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 -m chpc_ansible_helper
.I command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B chpc-ansible-helper
.I command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chpc-ansible-helper
builds Ansible playbooks on a machine with no network access and no AI
model involved at all -- the same tool as
.BR chpc-bash-helper / chpc-python-helper ,
generating a playbook (YAML) instead. You either pick a template from
its library and answer a short series of questions, or describe what
you want in plain English and let it match your description against
the library by keyword overlap.
.PP
Every template uses only
.B ansible.builtin
(ansible-core) modules -- no extra collections needed. Every generated
playbook is checked with
.B ansible-playbook --syntax-check
if available, or a plain YAML structural check otherwise; a value you
type is safely embedded as a quoted YAML scalar (via Python's
.BR json.dumps() ),
so special characters in your input can't corrupt the playbook's
structure.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List every template in the library.
.TP
.BI show " template-id " "[--raw]"
Show what a template asks. With
.BR --raw ,
also print the template's raw, unrendered text.
.TP
.BI describe " \(dqdescription\(dq"
Rank every template by plain keyword overlap against
.IR description .
.TP
.BI build " template-id " "[options]"
Build a playbook from
.IR template-id .
With no
.BR --var / --toggle / --toggle-group / --yes
flags, runs an interactive wizard; with any of those, runs
non-interactively.
.SH OPTIONS FOR "BUILD"
.TP
.BI --out " path"
Where to write the generated playbook. Defaults to
.IR template-id .yml
in the current directory.
.TP
.BI --var " NAME=VALUE"
Answer one variable non-interactively. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --toggle " NAME=on|off"
Answer one yes/no toggle non-interactively. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --toggle-group " NAME=VALUE"
Answer one multiple-choice group non-interactively. Repeatable.
.TP
.B --yes
Accept every default and run non-interactively.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 -m chpc_ansible_helper list
python3 -m chpc_ansible_helper describe "apply a firewall baseline"
python3 -m chpc_ansible_helper build firewall_baseline
python3 -m chpc_ansible_helper build node_drain_resume \e
    --var "NODE_LIST=node042" \e
    --toggle-group "SCHEDULER=slurm" \e
    --toggle-group "ACTION=drain" \e
    --out node042_drain.yml
ansible-playbook node042_drain.yml
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An unknown template id, a malformed
.BR --var / --toggle / --toggle-group
value, a template failed its syntax check, or the interactive wizard
was cancelled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I chpc_ansible_helper/library/*.json
Template metadata: title, description, tags, and declared
variables/toggles/toggle_groups.
.TP
.I chpc_ansible_helper/library/*.yml.tmpl
The matching raw playbook template text, with
.B {{VARIABLE}}
and
.B {{#TOGGLE}}...{{/TOGGLE}}
placeholders (no space inside the braces) alongside genuine Ansible
Jinja2 expressions such as
.B "{{ item }}"
(always with a space) -- the two never collide.
.TP
.I chpc_helper_core/
The shared engine this app is built on -- must be copied alongside
.I chpc_ansible_helper/
as a sibling directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full manual,
.IR CHPC_HELPER_SUITE_MANUAL.md ,
and this package's own
.IR README.md ,
both shipped alongside this tool.
.SH AUTHOR
Coastal HPC.
